# Strom for Eyevinn Open Source Cloud.
#
# The upstream release image, unmodified. Everything OSC needs is already in
# it: the server listens on STROM_PORT=8080, persists to STROM_DATA_DIR=/data,
# exposes 8080, and its entrypoint starts dbus and avahi-daemon for NDI
# discovery before exec'ing /app/strom.
#
# This file used to be a second copy of the upstream Dockerfile, ~180 lines of
# multi-stage Rust and Zig cross-compilation. Keeping a copy meant keeping it
# in sync by hand, and it had drifted five months behind: Ubuntu plucky (EOL)
# instead of questing, so it missed the nvcodec fix in gstreamer1.0-plugins-bad
# 1.26.3+; no gstreamer1.0-gl or EGL/GBM, so no CUDA-GL interop; no patched
# decklink plugin, so no capture-group property; no dbus/avahi, so no NDI
# discovery; and the backend built without the efp feature. Tracking the
# published image puts OSC on the same build everyone else runs, and takes the
# build from a ~40 minute cross-compile to a pull.
#
# `latest` follows the newest upstream release, so an OSC rebuild picks up
# fixes without a change here. Pin a version (eyevinntechnology/strom:0.6.8)
# instead if a reproducible build matters more than staying current.
#
# No entrypoint wrapper: a set-but-empty STROM_DATABASE_URL, which OSC
# forwards for an instance with no DatabaseUrl configured, is handled upstream
# as of Eyevinn/strom#738. Requires a release built from that commit or later.
FROM eyevinntechnology/strom:latest
